# Binary assets must round-trip byte-exact.
#
# GitHub Pages publishes the exported artifact verbatim, so a PDF, WebP or
# GLB that gets CRLF-rewritten on the way into the repository is corrupted
# for every visitor. Without these lines the behaviour depends on git's
# content sniffing plus core.autocrlf, which differs between a Windows
# checkout and the Linux runner that performs the deploy.
*.pdf binary
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.zip binary
